## 8. Final Recommendation to Present

Position the proposal as a two-phase migration strategy:

**Phase 1 — POC:** Export eligible source files from HDFS to an approved Linux landing zone, then transfer them to AWS S3 using a lightweight watcher/transfer worker and Gateway integration. Use this to validate connectivity, integrity, and AWS Merger compatibility.

**Phase 2 — Strategic Implementation:** Enhance the existing File Watcher and OneOps API to support configurable parallel delivery to HDFS and AWS S3, eliminating the additional HDFS export dependency.

Emphasize that Spark Structured Streaming remains appropriate for Kafka-based streaming ingestion and distributed data processing, but is not the default choice for simple file discovery and transfer.

The final proposal must be technically defensible, migration-focused, cost-conscious, and suitable for enterprise architecture review.

Avoid generic cloud migration recommendations. Focus specifically on the OneRec file ingestion architecture, existing OneOps API integration, HDFS-to-S3 migration, Gateway requirements, and AWS Merger readiness.
